Package: z3r
Title: Native R Interface to the Z3 Theorem Prover
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Adam R", "Sophie", email = "adamrsophie@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: An interface to the 'Z3' satisfiability modulo theories (SMT)
    solver <https://github.com/Z3Prover/z3> built directly on its native C
    API. Provides typed symbolic expressions over integers, exact rationals,
    Booleans, bit-vectors, arrays, strings and uninterpreted functions,
    natural R operator syntax, incremental solving, assumptions and
    unsatisfiable cores, optimization, quantifiers, tactics, and 'SMT-LIB2'
    import and export. Exact values are never silently rounded to double
    precision. This is an independent third-party package; it is not an
    official 'Z3' or Microsoft product.
License: GPL-3
URL: https://github.com/adamrsophie/z3r
BugReports: https://github.com/adamrsophie/z3r/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Language: en-US
Depends:
    R (>= 4.3.0)
Imports:
    Rcpp (>= 1.0.10)
LinkingTo:
    Rcpp
Suggests:
    gmp,
    knitr,
    rmarkdown,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
VignetteBuilder: knitr
SystemRequirements: Z3 (>= 4.8.12) C library and headers: libz3-dev
    (Debian, Ubuntu), z3-devel (Fedora), z3 (Homebrew), or an official Z3
    release archive
Config/testthat/edition: 3
